### Quest Lines ###

## GT Interesting Thing

betterquesting.questline.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQ.name=§6§lGT Interesting Thing
betterquesting.questline.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQ.desc=GTIT lays a cat-shaped economy over GregTech: the ops layer's vending machine, sign-in, lottery and mail; the tool layer's coins, float cores, infinite cells and eight rings.%n%n§133§r quests fork from one root — ops to the east, tools to the west — converging on quest-gated endgame trades.%n%n§8§oThe cat has taken over your economy, and is not planning to give it back.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQ.name=§6§lTwo Faces of the Cat Economy
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQ.desc=GTIT has two faces: the §3ops layer§r — vending machine, starter gift, sign-in, lottery and mail — and the §3tool layer§r — coins, float cores, infinite cells and eight rings.%n%nThe east branch runs the ops: build the machine, feed the wallet. The west branch runs the tools: let rings and cores work for you.%n%n§8§oThe cat has already taken over every corner of the economy. Resistance is futile.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAg.name=§6§lThe Cat Ops Deck
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAg.desc=The moment you first enter the world, the cat stuffs a §2starter gift§r into your hands — a persisted flag guarantees it happens exactly once.%n%nBetter yet, this layer is §2customizable everywhere§r: what goes inside the gift, what the shelves sell, what sign-in and the lottery pay — all customizable through their own configs, and an admin can flip on a §3visual edit mode§r to reshape shop entries right inside the GUI, no code required.%n%nHand the whole gift over for inspection; §2checked, not taken§r. §8§oThe urge to open it first is your own problem.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAw.name=§2§lUnboxing the Cat's Welcome Kit
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAw.desc=The gift's guaranteed list: §116 bread§r, §164 torches§r, a bed, §18 chests§r and §1one coin§r; beyond that, two rings are drawn at random — Skywalk, Ironheart, Dragon's Breath, Mountainbreaker or Tempest.%n%nMechanics first: the gift is granted §2automatically on first login§r, and a persisted flag keeps it strictly one-time. Customizing is one command away — §3/gtit gift certain§r seals your current inventory as the guaranteed items, §3/gtit gift random <count>§r as the random pool, and §3/gtit gift reset§r returns everything to defaults.%n%nWant a re-issue? §3/gtit gift claimreset <all|player>§r wipes the claim record (§3/gtit gift claimlist§r lists who has claimed) — the box re-arrives on that player's next login.%n%nSubmit a bed and a stack of torches as your receipt; §2everything stays yours§r. §8§oA second free lunch, hand-delivered by the cat.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABA.name=§6§lBuild the Cat Machine
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABA.desc=The Neko Vending Machine is the heart of the ops layer: trade, sign-in, lottery and mail all run from this one machine.%n%nAssemble it into shape and the input side simply takes your materials, while prizes stack into a §2virtual chute with no visible bottom§r — the hundred-slot output column is virtual, and no windfall will ever overflow it.%n%n§c§lNote:§r as a GregTech machine block it is verified by retrieval — get one into your hands first, then claim.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABQ.name=§d§lWiring the Cat into ME
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABQ.desc=The §dME Uplink Hatch§r replaces any casing block on the vending machine, and the whole machine takes §1at most one§r.%n%nOnce linked, produce and consume connect straight to your §dAE network§r: rewards flow into ME, materials are pulled from ME, and physical hauling becomes history.%n%nPresent the hatch for inspection — §2checked, not consumed§r — then slot it back in and keep working.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABg.name=§6§lWallets, Import and Teams
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABg.desc=Coins do not live in your inventory: drop them into an input slot, press import, and they become a §2virtual balance§r keyed to your §3UUID§r — or to your team's shared wallet.%n%nImports can pull straight from the §dAE network§r; ejection reverses the trick. Balances are atomic against double-spending and flushed every §15 minutes§r.%n%nOpen your wallet, count your blessings and tick this box — the cat only wants proof you have met real money.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABw.name=§2§lDaily Sign-In
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABw.desc=Open the calendar in the sign-in tab and click once a day: §110§r coins on weekdays, §120§r on weekends, with the streak coefficient locked at §11.0§r.%n%nStreak tiers pay once per tier each month; cumulative tiers stay §2valid forever§r — the longer your sign-in history, the deeper the wallet.%n%nCollect today's sign-in wages, then tick this box — §2a ceremonial audit, capital untouched§r.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACA.name=§8§lPaid to Idle
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACA.desc=Online-time rewards run three tiers, each claimable once per day: §130 minutes§r pays §15§r, §12 hours§r pays §120§r, §15 hours§r pays §150§r.%n%nTiers reset daily, and time only counts while you are actually on the server — §2idle long enough and it compounds§r.%n%n§8§oSponsored anonymously by the Cat Guild. All interpretive rights belong to the cat.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACQ.name=§d§lThe Roulette and Its Pity
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACQ.desc=The lottery runs two pools side by side: the Neko pool at §15 coins§r a draw, the Shimmering pool at §11 shimmering§r.%n%n§2The pity is real§r: from the §130th§r miss onward, every extra draw adds §15%§r weight to high-rarity entries; hard pity forces EPIC or better at §150§r draws on the Neko pool, §130§r on the Shimmering pool.%n%nNo entrance fee this time — tick the box and go spin your first draw; the wheel has been waiting.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACg.name=§6§lSaving for a Ten-Pull
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACg.desc=A single draw spins for §12.8 seconds§r; a ten-pull flashes for §11.4§r. The server dispatches prizes only after the animation plus a §1150 ms§r margin — no spoilers, ever.%n%nPity counts per §2team per pool§r: every draw by any member pulls the whole team closer to the guarantee.%n%nSave up your ten-pull fund, then tick the box. §8§oSuperstition is free; pulling is not.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACw.name=§3§lThe Cat Post Office
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACw.desc=The Mail tab is a real mailbox: §150 mails§r per player, up to §15 attachment stacks§r each, delivered even while the recipient is offline.%n%n§c§lIron rule:§r a mail with unclaimed attachments cannot be deleted — no misclick risk, no lost loot, hoard letters without fear.%n%nTick this box and wave at the post cat on your way out.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAADA.name=§2§lBirthdays, Festivals, Cake
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAADA.desc=Fill in your birthday (§1MM-dd§r format) and custom anniversaries on the memorial page of the sign-in tab; festivals are configured server-wide by the admin.%n%nWhen the day arrives, a blessing mail lands automatically — §2the birthday template even carries a cake§r.%n%nTick this box — the cat has confirmed its blessings meet production standards.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAADQ.name=§c§lServer Ops Appendix
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAADQ.desc=§c§lOps appendix — nothing here touches player progression.§r This volume is all about the cat's own things: the machine's trade entries, sign-in rewards and lottery pools, every one of them admin-customizable.%n%nThe cat recommends the §3visual edit mode§r: flip §3/gtit nekovm edit on§r and edit trade-group entries right inside the vending machine GUI — what you see is what you get, and §2/gtit nekovm reload§r makes it live in a second.%n%nTraditional command folks are not stopped either: the /gtit command family and the configs under §3§nconfig/gtit§r are all there; hand-writing JSON is your freedom. Quest gating accepts §3§nhigh:low§r, UUID or Base64. This line is an optional detour — skipping it costs nothing. §8§oThe cat does not care about your means, only that the shelves look good.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAADg.name=§6§lThe Player's Toolbox
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAADg.desc=Coins are everywhere: §1seven kinds§r of structure chests hold §12-8 each§r, and every successful catch carries a bonus coin about §110%§r of the time — a stack holds §164§r.%n%nThe Shimmering Coin is far more aloof: only a §12%§r bonus on the rod, with chest generosity and quest-hall rewards covering the rest.%n%nShow eight coins — §2checked, not taken§r — and push open the tool layer to the west. §8§oThe angler never blanks — in theory.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAADw.name=§6§lSixty-Four to One
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAADw.desc=This counter belongs to the §3built-in trade group§r: exchange §164 coins§r for §11 shimmering§r and walk your savings straight into the hard-currency club.%n%nCareful: the bare mod ships §cno exchange at all§r — the counter exists only through the built-in trade group, so do not go digging through the vanilla trade pages.%n%nPresent one shimmering coin for the check — §2display-verified, returned to the owner§r.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEA.name=§6§lThe Fifty-Six Spread
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEA.desc=The reverse counter sits in the same §3built-in trade group§r: §11 shimmering§r buys back §156 coins§r; 64 in, 56 out, and §18 coins§r quietly evaporate per round trip.%n%nThat eight-coin spread is §cseigniorage§r — the cat charges no fee, but the spread keeps both markets honest.%n%nTick the box and salute the arithmetic.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEQ.name=§d§lThe Infinite Cell
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEQ.desc=The infinite cell, registry name wearing its §ddouble gtit prefix§r: bytes pinned at §1INT_MAX§r, idle draw of a mere §61 AE/t§r.%n%nIt takes §1two§r upgrade cards plus partitioning; §cthe counter is the only source§r — the built-in group sells it at §132 shimmering§r apiece.%n%nSlot it into an ME drive and watch the capacity bar §2refuse to move§r, along with your storage anxiety.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEg.name=§d§lThe Infinite Fluid Cell
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEg.desc=The fluid twin of the infinite cell: same §1INT_MAX§r-class capacity, same §132 shimmering§r price at the built-in counter.%n%nThe structural difference is §1zero upgrade slots§r — no partitioning, no expansions; every slot serves the fluid itself, and simplicity is justice.%n%nSlot it in — §8§oyour lava ocean finally has a registered address.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEw.name=§2§lTake Flight on Steak
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEw.desc=Slot the Float Core into §3any accessory slot§r (Baubles universal) and §2creative flight§r is yours, at a cost of §10.02§r hunger per tick.%n%nDip below §16§r hunger and flight cuts out, dropping you back to earth. §c§lPilot's discipline:§r eat first, fly second.%n%nMake your first one by hand, then claim — §8§owings are earned one meal at a time.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFA.name=§6§lFuel for Flight
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFA.desc=Flight burns hunger, not fuel: steak is your §6aviation gasoline§r — a few bites and the range meter climbs back.%n%nKeep cooked beef on you at all times; the moment your hunger bottoms out always arrives one step earlier than planned — gravity never takes a day off.%n%nThese sixteen steaks will be §cactually collected§r: rest assured, they go to the cat's storeroom, not its stomach.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFQ.name=§6§lThirty-Two Million EU Wings
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFQ.desc=The Electric Float Core carries a §632M EU§r battery and flies on §6128 EU/t§r — the hunger bar finally moves to second place.%n%nCharging at §3LV§r draws §632 EU/t§r, a full tank taking about §114 game days§r; on empty it falls back to §10.01§r hunger per tick — exactly half of what the plain core burns.%n%n§8§oPatience is also a flight fuel; charging while you idle is part of the practice.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFg.name=§3§lThe Mind's Eye
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFg.desc=The Telekinesis Scanner Core sweeps §119x19 chunks§r (radius §19 chunks§r, §1144 blocks§r): ore and underground-fluid dual modes, toggled with §3Shift+right-click§r.%n%nEach scan demands hunger §1at 6 or above§r plus a one-time §124-point§r exhaustion hit; results push straight through §3§nVisualProspecting into JourneyMap§r as markers.%n%nMake one, and fit an entire geological survey team into a chest.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFw.name=§2§lFollow the Map
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFw.desc=The point of scanning lands on the map: ore and fluid markers spread out in clusters, §2legible at a glance§r, with not one line spammed into chat.%n%nThe correct workflow is planning your tunnels around the markers. §c§lWarning:§r copying coordinates out of the chat log line by line is so last era.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGA.name=§d§lLord of the Rings
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGA.desc=From now on, you have ten fingers! Your ring slots have grown to §110§r!%n%nRings are GTIT's fashion slots: with §3Baubles-Expanded§r loaded the ring row grows to §110 slots§r; without the library it quietly falls back to §12§r.%n%nSeven functional rings scatter across §1seven kinds§r of structure chests, at most §1one§r per chest. Too slow? The built-in counter sells them for §16-8 shimmering§r each — §2identical effect, zero chest luck required§r.%n%nEvery ring in this branch has its own page below — one finger at a time, go collect the set. §8§oTen fingers, ten slots; that is no coincidence.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGQ.name=§3§lDistant Grasp
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGQ.desc=Each Distant Grasp adds §1+2§r to your §1interaction and attack reach§r, stacking linearly — open chests from two blocks out, strike over fences; your arms just got longer.%n%nThe extension works silently at the engine level: no toggle, no keybind — equip to reach far, unequip and mortal range returns.%n%nPresent one Distant Grasp — §2checked, not taken§r. §8§oYou only learn the joy of long arms once something is finally within reach.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGg.name=§c§lIronheart
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGg.desc=Each Ironheart grants §1+20§r max health — a full §1ten hearts§r — stacking linearly: ×2 makes §1+40§r, and stacked high enough your health bar nearly leaves the screen.%n%nThe bonus settles in real time through §3attribute modifiers§r: equip to gain, unequip to lose, no ghost health bars left behind.%n%nPresent one Ironheart — §2checked, not taken§r. §8§oBeing a tank is its own kind of beef.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGw.name=§5§lDragon's Breath
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGw.desc=Wear the Dragon's Breath and four auras turn §2permanently on§r: §1Fire Resistance§r, §1Night Vision§r, §1Regeneration I§r and §1Resistance I§r — a §130-second§r batch auto-renewed every §15 seconds§r; the brewing stand can finally retire.%n%nSwim lava, dive into deepslate, face a raid head-on — all in perfect composure.%n%nPresent one Dragon's Breath — §2checked, not taken§r. §8§oA dragon's breath, a mortal's amulet.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHA.name=§2§lGluttony
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHA.desc=Gluttony feeds you nonstop: §1+1§r hunger per second; once the bar is full it switches to topping up §1saturation§r — sprinting and fighting barely make a dent.%n%nThe real ace is the emergency fill: the moment hunger drops below §15§r, hunger and saturation refill in one gulp, ready every §160 seconds§r — not even a lava plunge can starve you.%n%nPresent one Gluttony — §2checked, not taken§r. §8§oIts dictionary holds no hunger, only second helpings.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHQ.name=§d§lWindrider, the Final Ring
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHQ.desc=Seven rings converge into one, and the Windrider takes the stage: this final ring owes nothing to luck — §2gather the other seven rings§r and complete a grand convergence upon the crafting table.%n%nWhat emerges is §2creative flight at zero cost§r — the tale of eight rings sealed into a single promise: the sky is your default terrain from now on.%n%nForge it with your own hands, then go anywhere. §8§oPast the finish line is where the real map begins.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHg.name=§2§lQuests That Unlock Trades
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHg.desc=Three lines converge on the finale: shop entries can be quest-gated — §3§nhigh:low§r, UUID or Base64; unmet conditions keep the entry locked, while a missing BetterQuesting lets it pass safely.%n%nThe endgame pages rotate on §16h / 22h / 88h§r cooldowns, periodic trades read §1-1§r as unlimited%n%nTick this box, then go see what the cat stocked for you. §8§oThe cat never runs a loss-making deal — except this once.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHw.name=§b§lTempest
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHw.desc=Every §15 seconds§r, Tempest renews a §130-second§r dose for your legs: §1Speed II§r and §1Jump Boost II§r permanently online — no potions, no inventory space wasted.%n%nCommutes shrink, kiting gets mean, and one leap lands you on the roofline — your footsteps now carry wind.%n%nPresent one Tempest — §2checked, not taken§r. §8§oThe cat can no longer catch you; that is by design.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIA.name=§6§lMountainbreaker
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIA.desc=Mountainbreaker keeps two blessings of war permanently on: §1Strength II§r and §1Haste II§r, likewise renewed every §15 seconds§r for a §130-second§r cycle.%n%nOne ring, both answers: swing a pick and the ore vein blooms; swing a blade and the battlefield opens.%n%nPresent one Mountainbreaker — §2checked, not taken§r. §8§oA mountain is merely a mountain you have not broken yet.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIQ.name=§9§lSkywalk
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIQ.desc=Skywalk raises your step height to §11.1 blocks§r: a full block becomes as climbable as a slab — §2no jumping required§r; stairs, walls and wrinkled terrain all read as flat ground.%n%nNo more bumpy commutes, and scaffold-climbing during builds turns oddly gentle.%n%nPresent one Skywalk — §2checked, not taken§r. §8§oStairs are now purely decorative.§r
# BQ quests [pack=gtit] END

